From 94ee0ea6050d78e156e4d03ac4e7851b0825d22b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:08:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/23] BananaDS perf: direct-colour bitmap rows 16 pixels a
 NEON step (render.2d_conv16), and a prefetch toggle (render.2d_prefetch16)

ConvertRun16 (a direct-colour bitmap BG's row into the layer line) converted 8 pixels a step and folded every
converted pixel into acc/all (4 vector operations per 8 pixels, plus the horizontal reductions). Its callers only
test whether acc and all are zero, and an opaque pixel always carries the layer's non-zero flag, so the sources'
bit 15 tells the same: some pixel opaque, every pixel opaque. Now 16 pixels a step, two operations per 16 for the
test. rgds-sim (device build): ConvertRun16 175k -> 119k instructions a frame on membench 1x (0.314 -> 0.240 ms; main
thread -1.9%), and the 2D thread's 2d bucket -0.073 ms on dsstress-L5 at 2x. Exact: a random test against the old
function (200k runs, every n 0-256, opaque/transparent/mixed rows; a sabotaged copy is caught) and the pictures.
render.2d_conv16=off is the old loop.

render.2d_prefetch16 (off) prefetches the run's VRAM row and the next 512 bytes before converting, so their misses
overlap (~770 DRAM misses a frame on these ROMs); rgds-sim can't see prefetches yet, so it is a device verdict.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
